WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.039
- Do not drink the
airplane bathroom water.

00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:07.700
(funky upbeat music)

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.950
- Do people attempt to
join the Mile High Club?

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.490
Yes, it is a big fantasy for everyone.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.060
Everyone tries to give
you a little tip money.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.560
- Pretty sure I had passengers
give each other hand jobs

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.420
right in front of me.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.540
So what did I do?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.392
Well, offer 'em a warm towel.

00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:24.225
(laughs)

00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:25.970
- If you get caught doing
it, it's a big deal.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.140
It's a federal offense.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.280
- You get arrested, and you will be fined.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.920
You will be banned from the airline, and

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.650
no more flying for you to Mexico.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.130
Do flight attendants
talk about passengers?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.830
Yes, all the time.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.663
Oh my gosh.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:39.030
That's the first thing out of our mouth.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.110
- We always know what's
going on with our passengers.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.300
From the moment they step on that plane,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.610
there should be a greeter
up at the front saying,

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.610
welcome aboard, and at that moment we know

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.040
if we've got, you know,
a newlywed couple going

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.790
on their honeymoon, or somebody
who's a first time flyer

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.480
who says, I'm nervous,
I'm a first time flyer.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.300
Most of the time, they'll
tell us, or they'll give us

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.530
some type of cue.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.070
- First of all, when you're
boarding, we're always

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.750
checking you out, seeing
who's the sexy one,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.040
and then we rate, and like
okay, who's the hottest guy

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.920
in coach; or girl.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.610
Who's the hottest guy,
or girl in first class.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.210
And then who's the hottest
person in the whole plane.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.140
So if you see us in the
back talking and giggling

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.150
and looking at the
passengers, that's most likely

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.690
because I'm talking about you.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.620
What is potable water?

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.150
How is it used on a plane?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.669
- It's the water we
use for the lavatories,

00:01:27.669 --> 00:01:29.410
and for the coffee.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.243
The same water.

00:01:30.243 --> 00:01:32.370
I'll leave that up to you if
you wanna drink your coffee.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.190
- I wouldn't drink the coffee on a plane.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.960
They don't clean the tubes
where the water goes.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.620
So you're drinking all of that.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.180
So if you want water, get
it from the bottled water.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.140
- What is the dirtiest
part of an airplane?

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.720
Definitely the floor.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.170
The floor gets used and abused.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.410
People are walking all around that floor,

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.750
bringing stuff in, taking
stuff off, dropping things.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.740
- Do not walk barefoot on that airplane.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.240
Especially going to the lavatory.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.680
- Everyone's always
walking around barefoot,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.280
and getting like, fungus or something.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.770
- I see people walk in
barefoot in the lavatory

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.600
and I'm like, oh, that's
a lot of confidence.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.140
- Bring your own Chlorox wipes.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.890
No guarantee if those tray tables or seats

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.890
get cleaned after every flight.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.530
- In between flights, they
do clean, but what they mean

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.150
by cleaning is they vacuum
the carpet and, they do

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.710
wipe down the lavatories,
but every single tray table,

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:22.840
no, they don't wipe that down.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.770
They only do that only if
the plane is like, sitting

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.980
in the airport for like,
overnight or something.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.030
- How can a passenger
get into first class?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.830
Well, they can buy a ticket.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.218
- Upgrade your life.

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:34.330
(laughs)
Work harder.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.580
You gotta buy a ticket, man.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.450
There's just no way.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.790
- Or, they can ask a flight attendant.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.050
Never hurts to ask.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.600
If they can talk their
way into it, some of them,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.580
and they ask nicely, they
can get into first class.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.960
I've seen it done before.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.259
- We're not supposed to,
but if you're really cute,

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:56.040
we just say, hey, come over.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.710
I'd rather have you over here.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.490
- If you guys are gonna
be asking, you ask before

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.500
the plane takes off.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.540
- If you wanna get anything
free on an airplane,

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.520
it's actually pretty easy.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.300
Just be super nice to
your flight attendants.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.480
If you're having like, a
drink or two, I've met a lot

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.380
of flight attendants
that would just be like,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.840
oh, I'll come back and charge you later,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.960
and they never come back.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.740
- Are diet drinks the worst
drinks to order on a flight?

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:20.740
Diet cola is literally the
worst drink to pour on a flight.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.770
The bubbles, for some
reason, they never go down.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.710
They're so fizzy.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:27.500
So we'll open the can,
and pour it, and we'll

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.140
literally just wait.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.260
- That fizz takes so long
to de-fizz that I coulda

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.080
poured a whole plane drinks by the time

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.630
that Diet Coke de-fizzes.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.030
If you order a Diet Coke
with me, you'll probably

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.610
get the whole can, 'cause I
don't got time for all that.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.880
- Well, thanks for watching.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.320
Hopefully you learned some
important, helpful tips

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.730
for your next flight.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.010
Be nice to your flight
attendant, and b'bye.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:53.960
- Have a good day.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:54.843
- Good bye.

00:03:54.843 --> 00:03:55.890
(upbeat music)

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.100
- So be nice to your flight
attendants, just like

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.630
you would be nice to your
waitresses and puppy dogs.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.280
We're just there for your safety, dang it.

